  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499699549803_975803_44555" xmi:uuid="2261c4e1-4cf3-48d5-a030-4ab0e7310200" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510151134132_85478_31124" xmi:uuid="47597072-1c96-4b56-8480-95cf2889c5e3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499699549803_975803_44555"/>
      <body>This capability is for the representation of the data that identify a requirement and versions of requirements.&lt;br&gt; The concept of a "requirement" in this context, relates chiefly to the exchange and sharing of data between requirements engineering applications such as those used in the systems engineering and related industrial domains.&lt;br&gt; This capability also include the verification and validation used together for checking that a data meets requirements and that it fulfils its intended purpose. The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;Requirement_domainModel_Overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 Requirement and V&amp;V DomainModel&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
